{"name":"Neptune’s Wrath","hex":"#11425d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"neptune","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brass or copper pan used to evaporate salt water to obtain salt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neptune"},{"term":"wrath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Great anger;  an instance of this.","Punishment, retribution, or vengeance resulting from anger;  an instance of this."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To anger (someone); to enrage.","To become angry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Neptune","blocks":[{"text":"Neptune is the eighth and farthest known planet orbiting the Sun. It is the fourth-largest planet in the Solar System by diameter, the third-most-massive planet, and the densest giant planet. It is 17 times the mass of Earth. Compared to Uranus, its neighbouring ice giant, Neptune is slightly smaller, but more massive and dense. Being composed primarily of gases and liquids, it has no well-defined solid surface. Neptune orbits the Sun once every 164.8 years at an orbital distance of 30.1 astronomical units. It is named after the Roman god of the sea and has the astronomical symbol , representing Neptune's trident."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Neptune_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png/330px-Neptune_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neptune","wikidata":"Q332"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Neptune_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png/500px-Neptune_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Neptune_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png/500px-Neptune_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont